course: dictionary
lesson: 4490
title: Hateful and the words we choose
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hateful comes from hate. Something hateful is very unpleasant, and it hurts people. «Hateful comments about someone's skin colour or religion should be reported» tells you the comments are unkind and meant to hurt people.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. The sentence says the comments should be reported, so they must be something bad. Now test your meaning: «Hurtful comments about someone's skin colour or religion should be reported» still makes sense, so hateful means very unkind and unpleasant.
explain: Hateful can also describe a thing, not only a person. «This hateful rain» means the rain is horrible and nasty. This use is informal and a bit old-fashioned, so you may meet it in older stories. When you read it, ask yourself: is this about how someone feels, or about how something seems?
fact: Hateful means very unpleasant and deserving to be hated.
fact: «Hateful words» are unkind words meant to hurt people.
fact: Hateful comments aimed at someone because of who they are should be reported, not shared.
fact: Rabbi Hillel taught: «What is hateful to you, do not do to your neighbour.»
fact: Informally, hateful can mean horrible or nasty, as in «this hateful rain».
exercise: «Hateful comments about someone's skin colour or religion should be reported.» What should you do with hateful comments? | Share them with your friends | *Report them | Laugh at them and forward them | Save them to read again
exercise: Hillel taught: «What is hateful to you, do not do to your neighbour.» What is the lesson? | *Do not do to others what is hateful to you | Hateful is another word for friendly | Hateful things are fun to do to others | Always be hateful to your neighbours
exercise: Someone says «this hateful rain». What does hateful mean here? | Lovely and warm | *Horrible and nasty | Hard to see through | Glowing with light
test: Which phrase best describes «hateful messages»? | *Messages full of hate towards others | Long, detailed letters | Messages sent by post | Kind, happy messages
test: «After the match, three players were sent hateful posts online.» What is the right move with a hateful post? | Keep it secret and read it again | *Report it | Share it so everyone can see | Reply with a hateful post of your own
exam: The word hateful is closest in meaning to which word? | Bright | Quiet | *Nasty | Friendly
